]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. Node1 persistently serves the approved read-only boot tree, node2 retrieves byte-identical approved files, write and traversal attempts are rejected, and the original RHEL release and kernel are retained. Restart evidence is complete and consistent for both managed nodes. Only minor temporary-file residue reduces operational hygiene.","limitations":["The lifecycle collector inventories /tmp only by pathname, so it confirms residual test artifacts but not their final contents or aggregate size. Command outputs nevertheless show these were small transfer and negative-test files."]}
